    "in_flight_mass_model_note": "user decision 4 (2026-11-05, '이 배터리로 진행, 질량은 나중에 결정'): false = the pack, switch, leads and ties (and the material the switch hole removes from the top cap) are real CAD solids / lumped items for geometry and interference (C37-C39) and for the pending-mass report (extra.logic_power, cad/exports/logic_power_pending_mass_vtol.json / .md), but they stay OUT of the report's parts / totals - the mass / CG / inertia that the sim, the firmware headers and the mass targets consume (the top cap's mass entry is the cap without the logic switch hole, C40 proves it). true = they join the flight mass model; set it only after the user decides (then re-run the CAD, sizing, sim and firmware chain). Switch-collar round (2026-11-05): the protective collar printed with the cap (logic_power.collar) is behind the same switch - the flight-mass cap is the cap without the hole and without the collar."
